  "body": "Stacked on #1136 (→ #1131 → #560 → #551). Fork synced at v0.18.0. Until those merge, this PR's diff against `main` includes theirs; its own change is the last commit.\n\n## What changed\n\nA sinker EDM electrode is generated from the picked faces of a part's cavity - its level floor and every vertical wall standing on it - and added to the document as #541's electrode tool, in one undo step.\n\n- **`motion::sinker_cavity::cavity_of`** (pure, no world) reads a face set as one cavity. Each face is checked on its own (finite, in range, planar, non-zero area, closed boundary), classed by its outward normal, and the walls are matched to the floor's outer ring edge by edge: a wall stands on a floor edge when one of its edges lies on it at floor height and its normal points into the floor. Every floor edge must be covered end to end.\n- **`motion::sinker_electrode::derive`** offsets the outline inward by `undersize + orbit` with the geometry crate's polygon offset (`geo2d::Region::offset_sharp`, Clipper2) and extends the electrode a stated stub above the cavity's mouth. The sizes are the arithmetic `cavity - 2 x inset`; the offset polygon must agree within 10 nm or the derivation refuses.\n- **`standing_in`** clips the part's facets against the cavity's column above the floor: a boss, a rib or an overhang in the electrode's way refuses the electrode with the spot.\n- **`operation::sinker_faces`** resolves the picks (the one pick rule, #692; outward normals by the facets' winding) and reads a condition's undersize by id through #531's door.\n- **`commands::ElectrodeFromFaces`** is the undoable command (its write and inverse are `AddTool`'s). **MCP: `electrode_from_faces`** runs it; its reply carries a `burn` object that `add_operation`'s `params` takes as is.\n\n## Rectangular cavities only, for now\n\nThe stock sim burns an electrode with #541's box atom: an axis-aligned rectangular face. So only a cavity whose outline is an axis-aligned rectangle yields an electrode. A rounded corner, a rotated rectangle, an L, a curved wall, a drafted wall or a stepped floor is refused by name, and the refusal names the follow-up: **#1152** (a sim atom and a tool record for an electrode body). The offset outline is already computed and carried on the result for it.\n\nOrbit (#544) is not merged: an optional orbit radius is accepted and taken off the electrode, and the tool's answer says so. Until #544 changes #543's size law, a Sinker Burn judges such an electrode without its orbit.\n\n## Refusals, each by name\n\nEmpty face set · a face with a non-finite or out-of-range coordinate · a zero-area or degenerate face · an open loop (a boundary that does not close) · a curved (welded) or non-planar wall · a leaning (drafted) wall or tilted floor · a face looking down · no floor · two floors (faces from different cavities, or a stepped cavity) · only the floor · a wall of another cavity (stands on none of the floor's edges, reaches below it, or faces away) · walls that do not close around the floor · a self-intersecting outline · a non-rectangular cavity (#1152) · an inset that consumes the cavity · a garbled undersize, orbit, stub or pickup · picks on different models, on no part, a stale id, a chain or a vertex · an open, inside-out or non-manifold body · the part standing in the cavity's column · a taken or reserved tool name.\n\n## How tested\n\nRun one by one (`cargo test -p <crate> ... -- --exact` style), debug:\n\n- `camcraft-motion --lib sinker_electrode` (7 tests): `a_rectangular_cavitys_faces_yield_its_electrode`, `a_cavity_reads_whatever_the_winding_split_or_order`, `every_degenerate_face_set_is_refused_by_its_own_name`, `a_cavity_the_box_atom_cannot_burn_is_refused_by_name`, `the_model_standing_in_the_cavitys_column_is_found`, and the seeded fuzz: `fuzz_a_damaged_cavity_is_always_refused_by_name_never_a_panic` (6000 sound cavities, each then damaged one of 20 named ways and required to refuse by that name) and `fuzz_garbage_faces_never_panic_and_never_answer_a_nonsense_electrode` (20000 garbage face sets with NaN, infinities, `f64::MAX`, denormals).\n- `camcraft-app --test sinker_electrode` (8 tests): `a_pockets_faces_yield_an_electrode_that_burns_that_pocket_in_the_sim` (the generated rough leaves stock and gouges nothing, the generated finish leaves the program verdict clean), `the_verdict_convicts_the_generated_electrode_burned_off_its_point` (the contrast: 1 mm off centre gouges), `the_electrode_is_one_undo_step_and_its_name_is_checked`, `the_condition_door_reads_the_undersize_or_refuses_by_name`, `a_face_set_that_is_no_single_cavity_is_refused_by_name`, `faces_from_different_cavities_are_refused_by_name`, `a_boss_in_the_cavity_is_in_the_electrodes_way`, `a_rounded_pocket_is_refused_by_name_until_the_sim_burns_a_body`.\n- `camcraft-app --test sinker_electrode_mcp`: `the_electrode_is_generated_and_burned_over_mcp_with_the_gui_commands`.\n\nThe fuzz found one hole while this was written: a denormal stub vanished into the depth, giving an electrode no longer than its cavity. The stub now has a floor (1 micron) and the length is checked against the depth.\n\nGate (local, debug, head `c93678aa`):\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib`: 205 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test sinker_electrode --test sinker_electrode_mcp --test sinker_burn --test sinker_undersize --test mcp --test mcp_pick --test mcp_pockets --test mcp_order --test commands_undo --test tool_law --test pocket_recognition --test edm_conditions --test edm_machine`: 109 passed, 0 failed.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- **Not exercised on a real EDM control.** Synthetic conditions and parts built in code only (#290 D10).\n- No GUI entry: the sinker pages are #548's; the command is what its button will run.\n- The full quick-gate plan (every suite whose gate map names `app::commands` / `app::operation` / `app::mcp`, about 190 app binaries and 7 ui suites) was not run; the change is additive (new modules, one appended tool-table row, no existing function edited), and the suites named above were run instead.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill's tool table is a process file and is not touched here (`tools/list` is the live registry).\n- STEP-imported parts: the fixtures are meshes built in code. A wall that is off vertical by more than a millionth is refused as leaning.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/547-electrode-from-faces.md`.\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM: an electrode is generated from the picked faces of a part's cavity (its floor and walls), offset inward by the undersize and extended to a holder stub - `ElectrodeFromFaces`, MCP `electrode_from_faces`; rectangular cavities only, every other face set refused by name (#547)\n\nEffort: max (not escalated)\n\nFixes #547\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
